  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Grammar · khi nào and bao giờ (when?)",
     "texto": [
      "**khi nào** and **bao giờ** both mean «when?». Their position can guide the interpretation, but it does not mark the tense on its own: the context also counts, and expressions such as **sẽ** (future) or **hôm qua** (yesterday).",
      "At the start, **Khi nào bạn đi Đà Lạt?** usually asks about a future trip: «When are you going to Đà Lạt?». At the end, **Bạn đi Đà Lạt khi nào?** usually asks when something happened or happens: «When did you go / are you going to Đà Lạt?»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "mấy giờ and lúc mấy giờ (what time?)",
     "texto": [
      "**Mấy giờ rồi?** = what time is it?",
      "**Mấy giờ bạn đi?** and **Bạn đi mấy giờ?** ask what time you leave. The position alone does not decide whether it refers to the past or the future: the context makes it clear.",
      "**lúc** is like the English «at» before a time: **lúc tám giờ mười lăm phút** = at a quarter past eight.",
      "**lúc mấy giờ** means «at what time?» and appears in questions like **Bạn đi lúc mấy giờ?**. The position can vary depending on the sentence."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "sẽ + verb (the future)",
     "texto": [
      "**sẽ** before the verb marks the **future**: **Tôi sẽ đi làm** = I'll go to work.",
      "In informal conversation **sẽ** is often dropped if it is already clear that it is the future (for example, because «tomorrow» appears): **Ngày mai tôi đi làm** = tomorrow I'll go to work."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
